---

## What is NOT included in this repository

| Asset type | In this repo? | Notes |
|------------|---------------|-------|
| AD track audio files | No | Not redistributed. Uploaded via the admin portal to your own storage. |
| Reference audio (movie/TV soundtracks) | No | Copyrighted by the original rights holders. Not redistributed. |
| Fingerprint hash databases | No | Generated from reference audio. You must generate your own. |
| Poster images / stills | No | Copyrighted by the original rights holders. Not redistributed. |
| Title metadata (real titles, actors, etc.) | No | The admin portal manages your catalogue. No real metadata is included. |

---

## Your responsibilities when deploying DescribeAT

If you deploy the admin portal, you are responsible for:

1. **Sourcing audio description content** — either producing your own AD tracks or licensing them from content providers under whatever licenses apply in your jurisdiction.
2. **Complying with copyright law** — audio description tracks are derivative works of the original content. Ensure you have the legal right to produce and distribute AD tracks.
3. **Configuring your own storage** — all media content must be hosted on your own infrastructure (S3, CDN, etc.). The admin portal uploads to your configured S3 bucket.
4. **Managing your own Firebase project** — push notifications require a Firebase project with Cloud Messaging enabled. Your Firebase credentials are your responsibility.

